        "rating": 4,
        "relativeTime": "5 months ago",
        "text": "Level 6 (Coconut Grove) – Great food with stunning sunset view\n\nWe dined at Level 6 in Coconut Grove during our Miami trip and had a very enjoyable evening. We ordered the seafood paella and octopus leg, and both dishes were well-executed and flavorful — honestly among the better meals we’ve had in Miami.\n\nWe paired our dinner with a bottle of Daou white wine, which complemented the food nicely.\n\nThe restaurant is located on the rooftop, and the sunset view over Coconut Grove was beautiful, making the whole dining experience even more special. The bar area also looked inviting, and the overall ambiance was relaxed yet refined. Service was attentive and friendly throughout our visit.\n\nWould definitely recommend Level 6 for both food and atmosphere, especially around sunset.",
