  "LT South Beach": {
    "placeId": "ChIJq6rYZ5C02YgRbE7daLWhtvs",
    "address": "1440 Ocean Dr, Miami Beach, FL 33139, USA",
    "lat": 25.7864772,
    "lng": -80.1298405,
    "rating": 4.5,
    "userRatingsTotal": 798,
    "phone": "(305) 673-0044",
    "website": "https://www.thebetsyhotel.com/lt-restaurant",
    "priceLevel": 2,
    "openingHours": [
      "Monday: 7:00 AM – 10:00 PM",
      "Tuesday: 7:00 AM – 10:00 PM",
      "Wednesday: 7:00 AM – 10:00 PM",
      "Thursday: 7:00 AM – 10:00 PM",
      "Friday: 7:00 AM – 10:00 PM",
      "Saturday: 7:00 AM – 10:00 PM",
      "Sunday: 7:00 AM – 10:00 PM"
    ],
    "mapsUrl": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=18137862349801737836",
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Irina Milyukova",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocLCABtE8_qSIk2vORLEvF8m0TI2FKeFPLVnpu-qJpjOqXQR1gc=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "a month ago",
        "text": "We ended up at this restaurant by chance. The hotel had opened a rehearsal space where our children were practicing, so we decided to stay and have dinner. We ended up having a wonderful Fourth of July celebration! The food was delicious, the menu was excellent, and the service was outstanding. We will definitely be back!",
        "isSpiceMention": false
      },
      {
        "author": "Whitney Buckingham",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWvLBzgYaxBB4fduWqbPAHakN6GjDyCF_7I2mzPpGSdZcZLletqUw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "3 months ago",
        "text": "Wow! We just walked in for a late brunch and were very impressed by the entertainment (piano and vocals) as well as the POPOVERS! Amazing popover eggs benedict… filled with some really delicious ham, cheese, bacon, creamed spinach, and perfectly poached eggs and homemade hollandaise, all in the amazing LT popover. Drinks were also great. Very impressed with our impromptu visit.",
        "isSpiceMention": false
      },
      {
        "author": "Meghan Thompson",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWiw134k6GjuK_cEyjndcpfABP-iEYQtp691qEJzVIxQW1Ph5zD=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "5 months ago",
        "text": "Wow, from the moment we walked into the restaurant everything was phenomenal. We didn’t have a reservation, and Farzana immediately offered to check on a table for us. She sat us promptly and was so sweet. Our server Franco, paid attention to detail, made sure all of our food was amazing, and was always there when we needed something. On top of that the manager Ever, was so great. He made sure we were set up properly for our appetizer and served our salad onto our plates for us. He brought us purse hooks, and when we had an extra guest added to the table last minute, he didn’t hesitate to open up the table and invite him to sit down. From host to server to manager, it was such an amazing experience. From someone who works in hospitality I was highly impressed, 10 out of 10. They brought us desserts at the end which was the cherry on top. I will definitely be back. Love love love!",
        "isSpiceMention": false
      },
      {
        "author": "Rochelle Poe",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocLMuOoUwpTc-oif06TyA2030S0FjDAQ13yBSdSWqn5RhmlMGg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "a month ago",
        "text": "Stumbled in here on my first night in Miami and went back on my last night of the trip because it was so good!\n\nBest martini I've ever had in my life and it was so good with blue cheese olives. They also make a great cosmo and espresso martini. Every plate of food was delicious, flavorful, and well balanced. Highly recommend trying the watermelon salad, sushi, branzino, and chocolate lava cake desert.\n\nThe service was also top notch. It started raining and they extended the awning to fully cover us. Our server even gave us the bread recipe and a free ice cream token for their ice cream shop. Would go back when I'm in Miami again!",
        "isSpiceMention": false
      },
      {
        "author": "S",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocK60u59MrI6tA8KgKXNZT91-F4B-KMuLNypCib8yCSUADwgcSJf=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5",
        "rating": 4,
        "relativeTime": "4 months ago",
        "text": "LT Steak & Seafood has a lovely bar and lounge atmosphere with live music that adds great energy without being overwhelming. It’s a perfect spot for light bites and a relaxed evening. The staff is consistently warm and attentive—Katherine, in particular, is fantastic and always makes guests feel welcome.\n\nFood-wise, the shrimp cocktail is excellent and a standout. The spicy tuna nigiri on crispy rice is a good dish as well, though it can be inconsistent—on occasion it’s been served soggy and cold.\n\nOne ongoing issue has made it difficult for me to fully enjoy the space. The restaurant allows non-service animals indoors in the bar area where food is served. There is a table frequently reserved for a guest with multiple large dogs, and when they are present, I’ve had to leave due to asthma and severe allergies, which makes it difficult for me to safely remain in the space. I have also observed staff petting the dogs and then returning to food service, which raises hygiene concerns and may not align with health code standards.\n\nI hope management will reconsider this policy and enforce a no non-service animals rule indoors, or at minimum create a clearly designated pet-free indoor area. I would gladly return more often if this were addressed.",
        "isSpiceMention": false
      },
      {
        "author": "Mariana Saad",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJjFXe1rzMExs18XcIw-PsMcziNN3LLRK66PbD12Cr7s3em=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4",
        "rating": 3,
        "relativeTime": "in the last week",
        "text": "Vinimos a ver jazz y había un señor tocando el piano. La comida regular. La Burrata y el pan estaban buenas , el crab cake desastroso y la burger muy regular.\nDefinitivamente es solo para tomar algo. No lo recomiendo para la cena",
        "isSpiceMention": false
      },
      {
        "author": "Mariam Razeghi",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVvCh3W2l7v0YCh5vh8aYz1QeywLWSaTHui44IiGiWq0gAtvDg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "a week ago",
        "text": "Wow - what an absolutely wonderful experience we had here! The food and drinks were fabulous, the kitchen and bar are turning out exquisite food and drinks, no doubt about it.\n\nBut I want to highlight the service here. From the gentleman holding the door as you’re welcomed into the dining room, to the hostess whom I observed going above and beyond to help guests and non-guests alike.\n\nWe were taken care of by Joanny during our 2025 visit and I hope we see her for our return in 2026. Joanny was great at timing our starters and entrees, she checked on us throughout the evening without overdoing it. She just knew when to stop by. She was so helpful answering questions about the menu and making suggestions. We asked about a special cocktail and later, when the bar had mistakenly made an extra, she offered it to us.\n\nAt the end of the night, we asked to speak to a manager to share our fantastic experience and Amy came to speak with us. She shared that she and Victor were part of the management team and she thanked us for sharing how awesome we found all the team members we encountered to be and how great the food and drinks were.\n\nWe’re looking forward to enjoying dinner here again in a few weeks. Book the table - you won’t regret it.",
        "isSpiceMention": false
      }
    ]
  },
