  "Manoli": {
    "placeId": "ChIJ4U3TQjy32YgRzqeyiakcs4M",
    "address": "3540 Main Hwy, Coconut Grove, FL 33133, USA",
    "lat": 25.7252435,
    "lng": -80.2450629,
    "rating": 4.8,
    "userRatingsTotal": 33,
    "phone": "(754) 285-5702",
    "website": "https://manoligreek.com/",
    "priceLevel": null,
    "openingHours": [
      "Monday: Closed",
      "Tuesday: Closed",
      "Wednesday: 5:00 – 10:00 PM",
      "Thursday: 5:00 – 10:00 PM",
      "Friday: 5:00 – 11:00 PM",
      "Saturday: 5:00 – 11:00 PM",
      "Sunday: 5:00 – 10:00 PM"
    ],
    "mapsUrl": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=9489960354285004750",
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "David Graham",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocLMqMIUgasw-uLeGJoE8BPOcwaOgY5cIfoqrSAXjz7B0Iqt6A=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
        "rating": 4,
        "relativeTime": "in the last week",
        "text": "I really wanted to like this new addition to the Grove but sadly it was a bit bumpy (as can happen for a new restaurant) and most notably fell short on a main and no-one there seemed bothered or asked how the dinner was at the end.  After an enjoyable cocktail (a milk punch), we ate off the Miami Spice menu.\n\nFirst course was an Octopus dish and a shrimp dish. Both excellent. Presented in serving dishes and plates available nearby, but the serving dishes placed between knife and fork. My wife burnt her hand on the hot metal serving dish with the shrimp (as she tried to eat from it). After some shuffling to set them properly, we ate and really enjoyed both. The tomato-based sauce in particular had great depth of flavor.\n\nThen came a main of Salmon and one of Lamb. On ordering we agreed with the waiter that the lamb would be medium rare. it was served well-done. Two small cutlets (seems they reduce the portion for Miami Spice as another post shows three). Waiter asked how it was and I showed him it was overcooked. I didn't send it back as the first one tasted OK but the other one even more overcooked, tough, not enjoyable and uneaten. Informed again on plate clearance. No follow through. Potatoes great. Overall main not up to anticipated standard or value.\n\nDessert of Orange cake and a frut salad was enjoyable.\n\nI would have given this feedback prior to leaving if asked, but no-one seemed to care or ask. One can only compare to other restaurants like Ariete and be reminded why they have such high ratings, and Manoli has a way to go. I'm very mixed on whether its worth another try.",
        "isSpiceMention": true
      },
      {
        "author": "Paulina Rodriguez",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjU4pbq0KgjwTNWGicgDeqwoZvr_Yowtw723H0cUbdR_iRy4CZ9A6g=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "in the last week",
        "text": "If I could give more stars I would!!!! I have never been to a restaurant with such incredible intentionality, service that was above and beyond, and a GENUINE care for their customers. Food was amazing, drinks are even better! Such an awesome atmosphere and experience!!! (I only spent $100 because my friend and I were there for FIVE HOURS— we were too obsessed we couldn’t leave!!!)",
        "isSpiceMention": false
      },
      {
        "author": "Mili",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJ7NKV4IypuIZv5p8DVOe7zn7dDd3FpG9FxQ7fcyWcf8zs0zXw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "in the last week",
        "text": "New neighborhood gem, great talent, food is fantastic. Ethan is the man. Thank you guys. Will be back for more.",
        "isSpiceMention": false
      },
      {
        "author": "Tom Noel",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjV92d_NP3QDiRcduhBmS7jIAFO7d_r4ZM6dq1mp_YtrXWD6E4pp=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "in the last week",
        "text": "Great ambience, attentive service, spectacular  Hummus sampler ,Tuna tartar  Back Angus meatballs! Will definitely be back!!",
        "isSpiceMention": false
      },
      {
        "author": "Banu Enes",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVrvzbemAuxEjb1iSPcsP7vXgyUL9axyeKyHqmKHxaPjW-sAA5aAw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "in the last week",
        "text": "After so long finally found a quality and perfect service restaurant in Miami. I love the fact that from the owner to the chef everyone welcomes you when you enter. All the staff are super friendly, welcoming and quick service which we don’t see it in Miami too often anymore. I also love the amazing dishes which made me feel l am in Greece. I will definitely make Manoli as my to go list when l miss the real Mediterranean food. Plus the atmosphere is awesome with the decor and Greek music",
        "isSpiceMention": false
      },
      {
        "author": "Anastasios Stamidis",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWFSiTN5d-TKcadpay9WPTd3dIXVK4J7ixGcXz8O1uMocaqoTiM=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "in the last week",
        "text": "Chef Manoli was great and very accommodating! Food was amazing and as a Greek in Miami it’s a place I will definitely go back. Vibe is great and plays Greek music too",
        "isSpiceMention": false
      },
      {
        "author": "Jessica Montoya",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVzWpjiaascX4RCfBvIdfGYhOcFseG_9JUQDsrs9G3yGntRKn0Lew=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "in the last week",
        "text": "We had such a wonderful experience at Manoli’s in Coconut Grove! From the moment we arrived, everything felt welcoming and thoughtfully done. The restaurant itself is beautiful, with an amazing atmosphere that feels elevated yet still warm and inviting. It’s such a great spot for a nice dinner in the Grove.\n\nThe food was absolutely delicious. Everything we ordered was fresh, flavorful, beautifully presented, and you could really tell there was attention to detail in every dish. The drinks were great as well, and the combination of the food, ambiance, and service made the entire evening feel special.\n\nOur server, Jonathan, was attentive, friendly, and made sure everything went smoothly throughout our dinner. The entire staff was welcoming and made us feel well taken care of from beginning to end.\n\nWe had a great night and will definitely be returning",
        "isSpiceMention": false
      },
      {
        "author": "Sarah Joseph",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJtqFQF21cF4oXrzRj1OjSrdwdhesVGdhRftbvXHSTPzQDMFA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "in the last week",
        "text": "Manoli is a fantastic addition to Coconut Grove and, in my opinion, even better than Meraki.\n\nEverything we ordered was exceptional. We started with the grape leaves, grilled octopus, and artichokes, followed by the whole grilled branzino served with Swiss chard on the side. Every dish was fresh, beautifully prepared, and full of flavor. I was especially happy to see they serve Mastika, my favorite Greek liqueur—it was the perfect complement to the meal.\n\nThe service was outstanding: warm, friendly, attentive, and professional throughout the evening. The dessert cart was a wonderful touch, and the baklava was one of the best I've had.\n\nOverall, this was an excellent dining experience, and we'll definitely be back. If you're looking for authentic Greek food with exceptional service in Coconut Grove, Manoli is a must-visit.",
        "isSpiceMention": false
      }
    ]
  },
