        "rating": 4,
        "relativeTime": "5 months ago",
        "text": "Came for Valentine’s Day and tried the special menu. The shrimp with mango appetizer was good but a bit simple in flavor. The ossobuco was excellent, rich, delicious, and full of flavor. The risotto was tasty but slightly undercooked and a little hard.\nThe chocolate brownie with raspberries wasn’t worth it (chewy and served cold), but the entraña was amazing, very tender and cooked perfectly.\nFirst time visiting. Our table was a bit low, but the ambiance was relaxed yet elegant. Staff was well dressed, attentive, and helpful. Overall, great service and a solid experience.",
