        "rating": 3,
        "relativeTime": "6 months ago",
        "text": "Walked in at 545 and was told I couldn’t be seated since I didn’t have a reservation. I turned around and made a reservation on my phone which were abundant. Turning back around I show the hostess my reservation and she asks me to wait until a table is ready. About 7 minutes later we are seated. Service by Megan r was very warm and friendly. 2 sushi rolls we ordered were delicious but unfortunately the rest of our order was lack luster. Herbs and dressing on Shisito peppers don’t add anything, mushrooms were ok. Salad was tasty but nothing mind blowing. We left most of our food and wish we had ordered more sushi rolls.",
