        "text": "ate at the IL Bolognese restaurant for two days and was pleasantly surprised by the quality.\nOn the first night, the linguine seafood pasta was excellent — fresh, flavorful, and I finished the whole plate. On the second day, I tried the lobster ravioli, which was rich and delicious but had a very large portion that was hard to finish. I also had tiramisu, which was creamy and satisfying.\nOverall, the food is above average for a hotel restaurant, especially the seafood dishes, but portions are quite big.",
