  "Andres Carne de Res Miami": {
    "placeId": "ChIJOZIFBwC12YgRieEn821YBic",
    "address": "455 Lincoln Rd, Miami Beach, FL 33139, USA",
    "lat": 25.7908027,
    "lng": -80.13305369999999,
    "rating": 4.7,
    "userRatingsTotal": 4800,
    "phone": "(786) 843-5910",
    "website": "https://andresmiami.us/",
    "priceLevel": 4,
    "openingHours": [
      "Monday: Closed",
      "Tuesday: Closed",
      "Wednesday: Closed",
      "Thursday: 4:00 – 11:00 PM",
      "Friday: 12:00 PM – 2:00 AM",
      "Saturday: 12:00 PM – 2:00 AM",
      "Sunday: 12:00 – 11:00 PM"
    ],
    "mapsUrl": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=2812032246593610121",
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Maryam",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjV409HoD_k3VXyA65f8NLNC5kOiQMZ8murXreWLBiFUFGTnczrt=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "3 months ago",
        "text": "We had a great experience at Andrés Carne de Res. We tried the empanadas, seafood pasta, burgers, and tuna tartare, and all of them were delicious.\n\nWhat really makes this place special is the vibe and atmosphere. There was live music, lots of energy, and such a fun and lively environment throughout the night. You can really feel the good atmosphere flowing through the whole place.\n\nI also celebrated my birthday here, and the staff surprised me with a traditional Venezuelan style celebration with music, dancing, and even confetti, which made the night so fun and memorable.\n\nDefinitely a great place if you want both good food and an exciting night out in Miami Beach!",
        "isSpiceMention": false
      },
      {
        "author": "Paul Echevarria",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWjyJz1CPMmPpE4j3tSsrM42MQ7p-YQN8J8kLJ2eKvQYhxzMvKq=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5",
        "rating": 4,
        "relativeTime": "3 months ago",
        "text": "Good food and atmosphere.  The price is a bit high for what you get but its expected for South Beach. They had music for about 45 minutes on a Sunday for what they promote as their Happy Hour special from 3-7PM. But that's it the music doesn't come back until around 8PM. That's a little boring for a happy hour. Also if you dont ask for the Happy hour menu they won't offer it. You have to ask for it. Very small Happy hour menu but it's the principal., if you are there for Happy hour they should give you the menu for Happy hour. Also the waiter even tho nice didn't know much about the Colombian culture when asked about certain items of the menu as a simple coffee he wasn't knowledgeable enough to know the difference between a Colombian coffee and an espresso.  Flavor was great and portions where as expected.  Fun birthday celebration if you celebrate your birthday as per video attached and they receive tou with a nice sign at your table if tou made reservations wich are recommended. Parking is recommended in a parking garage about 1 block away and will be about $5 per hour. One thing to be in the lookout. When they bring the bill they include 20% already and the waiter will try and get you to give an extra 20% stating the first 20 is to share amongst all the staff and the next 20 is for him. Be carefull. This can be a very costly mistake.",
        "isSpiceMention": false
      },
      {
        "author": "Julian Noviello",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUlrraihUlMwub-dp1zbJFUKI1DhmfB49jb746vEjkb0HNI7jnw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "2 months ago",
        "text": "From the moment you walk in, the place and the whole experience feel warm, welcoming, and captivating. Once inside, it becomes even more fascinating, and to crown it all, the food is simply impeccable. I’m not lying when I say that after living in Miami for 4 years, this is the first time I’ve truly eaten FOOD: full of flavor, seasoning, and every bite better than the last.\n\nI highly recommend starting with the octopus — absolutely sublime — and the arepa de choclo. For mains, we had the seafood pasta and the sea bass, both incredibly delicious. And to finish, ordering the Tres Leches dessert is mandatory.\n\nThe atmosphere, music, and food were perfectly complemented by the outstanding service from Manuela, who was attentive, warm, and thoughtful in every detail to make our experience flawless.\n\nWhether you’re a local or a tourist, everyone is obligated to experience and taste what Andrés Carne de Res is all about.",
        "isSpiceMention": false
      },
      {
        "author": "Noemi Herrera",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJKDEri1jxkTbnvb_JiYOn5w6WfdAsMeNUvni1wCsCHoA_j=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3",
        "rating": 4,
        "relativeTime": "4 weeks ago",
        "text": "We planned to go there and reserved weeks in advance. It was stated there would be a show going on of people singing and good music, it was cancelled due to the game going on, we were not told till we asked when we got there, it was a bummer but we watched the game. They have a cute photo booth there to take pics (they charge). The restroom was clean, only one. They come sing to you and clap, give you cake or wine depending on the celebration occasion. Also my plate was hellaaa good, though not the best picture.",
        "isSpiceMention": false
      },
      {
        "author": "Glen Trebilcock",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocIBLmTv4TN5ks97BRt-iWz-be2iOaB6nfN6YiZbUuhovqKCcTsw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6",
        "rating": 2,
        "relativeTime": "2 months ago",
        "text": "The best quality item (and quite frankly the only one) is the live band: perfect mood, vibe leadership and musicianship. Perhaps this place would work best as a standalone concert hall, without the attached restaurant!\nThe food was not bad, but our party of four got served as each plate came out of the kitchen, so my sea bass was served after my wife had long finished eating her “lomo al trapo”. We were much unimpressed by the service in general, subpar for the price.\nThe InKind app offers a $50 off $150 which sounds like a great deal, until you notice the 20% mandatory (and strongly undeserved) gratuity, which significantly reduces the benefit of the deal.\nWe had a good time, but do not wish to return in the future.",
        "isSpiceMention": false
      },
      {
        "author": "Veronica Muñoz",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjU-J4oQZ0zuYJFZtYIXfIvoHDq3IU0BbSJ8EH2ALJRxnhuQNYtMQQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "in the last week",
        "text": "Excellent place, great service, beautiful setting, native decor, delicious food!!!",
        "isSpiceMention": false
      },
      {
        "author": "Andrea C.",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjV5aXbrG5g5EWuVzg4L7OERDX6vRvz3BaHBwnULsvwI1AVJdnanjw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "in the last week",
        "text": "Manuela tiene una atención espectacular!!!\nSuper agradable el ambiente y la comida 100/10",
        "isSpiceMention": false
      }
    ]
  },
