        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "8 months ago",
        "text": "Upscale restaurant connected to a Michelin rated hotel. It’s in the Art Deco area of South Beach. We saw a number of fine restaurants but we chose this one because it was quieter. Their menu advertised the branzino as whole, and it was before they cooked it. Regardless of the semantics it was absolutely delicious although slightly over spiced which hid the flavors of the delicious fish. We started with an amazing grilled octopus that was tender and flavorful. My wife had the hangar steak cooked to a perfect medium rare.  We paid over $300 for our meal with drinks. It was worth it even if the service level didn’t quite match the exquisite meal. Everybody was polite and helpful just need a little training in how to serve high end dining.",
