        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "2 months ago",
        "text": "This was an amazing dinner with my wife. A hidden gem in the bussy South Beach. Soon as we arrived we were greeted with a smile and invited to our table. The server greeted us immediately and asked if we were there for the first time. After a brief presentation of the place and the specials he made recommandations for drinks and appetizers. It was a Wednesday night and the place already had customers. The music was upbeat and the atmosphere was vibrant, happy. The food started to arrived minutes later at the table. Presentation and flavors were on point. Chef Michael was on the expo checking the visual of every plate! Im a big fan of Italian cuisine and i was really impressed by the flavors and textures of the food! We finished our meal with a delicious Hazelnut Sundae and some chocolate liquor. We didn't felt rushed. Everyone was so attentive at the detalis, from the busses, foodrunners to the manager who came to check the satisfaction. We will definitely come back!!!",
        "isSpiceMention": false
