  "CalaMillor Gourmet Experience": {
    "placeId": "ChIJk7sD77252YgRguFsa5PaR04",
    "address": "4000 SW 57th Ave, Miami, FL 33155, USA",
    "lat": 25.733831,
    "lng": -80.2867692,
    "rating": 4.6,
    "userRatingsTotal": 1345,
    "phone": "(305) 456-3938",
    "website": "https://calamillormiami.com/",
    "priceLevel": 2,
    "openingHours": [
      "Monday: 8:00 AM – 9:00 PM",
      "Tuesday: 8:00 AM – 9:00 PM",
      "Wednesday: 8:00 AM – 9:00 PM",
      "Thursday: 8:00 AM – 9:00 PM",
      "Friday: 8:00 AM – 10:00 PM",
      "Saturday: 8:00 AM – 10:00 PM",
      "Sunday: 8:00 AM – 9:00 PM"
    ],
    "mapsUrl": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=5640717385002180994",
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "July Soto",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUPbB8lsOh6vwS0EtI5l_eENdHZ17kn-d5gpOdPLBuLyzBZBPxvJA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "a month ago",
        "text": "I normally do not give 5 stars for a first time experience at any restaurant, but Cala Millor in Coral Gables blew it out of the park for my first experience! What a pleasant experience it was. From the moment we arrived, we were greeted promptly by two enthusiastic ladies, one of which walked us to our table. Seconds later, our waiter, Carlos, came to us offering something to drink. My wife opted for water, and I ordered a latte, that in my opinion was one of the best I've had in a long while. We ordered, our food, which was exquisite and the perfect portions. My wife had the Salmon tartare with avocado and I ordered Huevos rotos con Chorizo. We also tried the ham croquets and churros with a side of melted chocolate and caramel. Everything was absolutely delicious. But one of the things that made our first visit more special, was the wonderful service provided by our waiters Carlos and Denise. We will certainly return to this restaurant and will highly recommend it to friends and family. Thank you all for this wonderful experience. Wishing you a long successful future so we can continue enjoying your establishment.",
        "isSpiceMention": false
      },
      {
        "author": "Leticia Murguey",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVUI_WKoTp1dzGPgrrBUD1ZpzZGth-JcvzK7TgaOJxvYVub4IcpMQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "8 months ago",
        "text": "What an excellent experience! I can’t express enough how much I loved celebrating our office party at CalaMillor! The service was outstanding — we truly had the best servers in Miami. The food was amazing! For me, the fideuà is the best dish ever, even better than the paella. The Basque cheesecake is dreamy, and the huevos rotos are to die for. Highly recommend!",
        "isSpiceMention": false
      },
      {
        "author": "Maria S",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocI8-BSF2dm-mPmth5qnGmmDHwQ-sMjaIG7lR-dm8DhYm60yZQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "2 months ago",
        "text": "Having just returned from Spain, we were looking for a way to relive the incredible food and dining experiences we enjoyed there, and Cala Millor exceeded all our expectations.\n\nFrom the moment we arrived, our server, Jacqueline, made us feel welcome. Since it was our first visit, we asked for her recommendations, and every single one was spot on. We started with the eggs, potatoes, and Iberian ham, along with the gambas and the delicious croquetas. Each dish was authentic, flavorful, and beautifully prepared.\n\nTo drink, we had the Gitana, their refreshing take on a white sangria, which was outstanding. For dessert, we tried their specialty cheesecake, and it was the perfect ending to an exceptional meal.\n\nEverything we ordered was fantastic, but what truly made the experience memorable was the outstanding service. Jacqueline’s knowledge, enthusiasm, and attention to detail elevated the entire experience.\n\nWe left thoroughly impressed and will definitely be back. Highly recommended!",
        "isSpiceMention": false
      },
      {
        "author": "Elizabeth Pascual",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVUL4Qm5Lul_bC6h_Dbjhy1HqSJMihGtLuKxhTNAY0izuk3iLMn=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "3 months ago",
        "text": "I had such an incredible experience at Cala Millor. From the moment I walked in, everything felt elevated. Beautiful ambiance, welcoming energy, and a level of attention that immediately stood out.\n\nThe food was just as impressive. The croquetas were absolutely delicious, perfectly crispy on the outside and flavorful inside. The pulpo con salsa verde was outstanding, so much so that I had to take another order home with me. I also came early one morning for breakfast and had the salmon avocado toast, which was fresh, beautifully prepared, and honestly one of the best I’ve had.\n\nI left feeling confident, refreshed, and beyond satisfied with my experience. It’s rare to find a place that consistently delivers both exceptional service and a great overall vibe, but Cala Millor absolutely does. I can’t recommend them enough—this is definitely a go-to spot in Miami!",
        "isSpiceMention": false
      },
      {
        "author": "Issy's Foodie",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUqj_orCdXJ_2a2QR24X6qrdJvQH_t5w7Y1p_pbQxDNY3ov8Y-M=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6",
        "rating": 4,
        "relativeTime": "5 months ago",
        "text": "So really good food and service.  The salmon tartare was spectacular.  The croquets  were delish all i tasted was really good.  Now the potato of chorizo tortillas are just superb.  Why 4 stars well they have a charge to use credit cards and we were not advised of it. And yes many places are doing this but so fat they all have advised of the fee.  All an all i will recomend the place.",
        "isSpiceMention": false
      },
      {
        "author": "gloria maria garzon ferrer",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocKbeepJZZ1MEzPdk6fLZNZ8ZZoOzeFQ-RdWRvpoZwVTQkl7pg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "in the last week",
        "text": "Exceptional!!!! Highly recommended.",
        "isSpiceMention": false
      },
      {
        "author": "Juan Giordano",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWpcTm1Hv-z1ZALFlfaX0ty1YvmyLUnz4DHb9FEkPJ5nw_C1TeJfA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "in the last week",
        "text": "Consistently great breakfast spot in the west side of Coral Gables.  Always friendly, se habla español.  JuanMi my longtime friend and server is always ready for us.  Don’t miss the CroqueMadame if you are a friend of truffle sauce… it has it all, fried egg, iberico ham, cheese and a lovely croissant holding it all together.  I am a regular here and just realized had not done a review…",
        "isSpiceMention": false
      },
      {
        "author": "Debbie Etter",
        "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocKG0IleSaIsidI8xfEfmK_RBgbwOKQET03JElzu94Ft_eZeOA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2",
        "rating": 5,
        "relativeTime": "a week ago",
        "text": "This was my first experience. Very charming. Little shopping area of novelties. Plus the bakery cases. I felt the food was very good. We had a bread with a red pepper olive oil that was excellent. The patatas bravas were okay but nothing like you get in Barcelona. Also had the branzino which was very good and fresh and I had the rice mushroom dish which was very good as well. Waitress very delightful only little caveat was had to keep asking her to fill the wine glasses when they were empty. But overall very good to exceptional. Recommend trying it at least once.",
        "isSpiceMention": false
      }
    ]
  },
